    pm:nameRole "one of the forty-two gods of the hall of the two Maati" ;
    skos:altLabel "usekh (Papyrus of Ani, 1895, as read)"@en ;
    skos:definition "The first address of chapter 125 in the Papyrus of Ani. Budge renders the name strider. The god is addressed as coming forth from Annu, and the address is bound to one denial: I have not done wrong."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:EgyptianRitual ;
    dcterms:source "Book of the Dead, chapter 125, the address to the forty-two gods, address 1, Papyrus of Ani, in the transliteration and English of E. A. Wallis Budge, London: British Museum, 1895, plates XXXI-XXXII, pp. 198-203" ,
        "Budge, A Hieroglyphic Vocabulary to the Theban Recension of the Book of the Dead, London: Kegan Paul, 1911, s.v. Usekh-nemmet, p. 115" .

